      "id": "DS1SZctgONA",
      "title": "A swim in the Strait of Hormuz amid tanker strikes to highlight war’s threat to marine life",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-21T11:55:30Z",
      "durationSec": 144,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/DS1SZctgONA/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "Endurance swimmer and United Nations Patron of the Ocean Lewis Pugh completed a 15-kilometre swim in the Strait of Hormuz to highlight the threat strikes on tankers pose to the region’s marine wildlife, coastline and coral reefs. The swim began on the Musandam Peninsula and took three days because strikes on oil tankers disrupted it. \n\nJoel Evans reports for Al Jazeera.\n\nSubscribe to our channel  http://bit.ly/AJSubscribe\nFollow us on X: https://X.com/AJEnglish\nFind us on Facebook https://www.facebook.com/aljazeera\nCheck our website:  http://www.aljazeera.com/\nDownload AJE Mobile App : https://aje.io/AJEMobile\n@AljazeeraEnglish\n#Aljazeeraenglish\n#News",
      "chapters": []
