    {
      "id": "YmYPIrXxtKc",
      "title": "What the ICJ ruling against Myanmar means for Rohingya refugees",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-21T10:46:40Z",
      "durationSec": 149,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YmYPIrXxtKc/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh’s Cox’s Bazar celebrated after the International Court of Justice ruled that Myanmar had breached its obligations under the Genocide Convention. The International Court of Justice said, in its ruling, that the killings and widespread sexual violence against the Muslim minority in 2017, amounted to state-sponsored genocide. The ruling is legally binding, but enforcement remains a challenge. \n\nRefugees are calling for accountability for the killing of relatives, compensation for homes and property that were burned, and the restoration of their citizenship rights.  \n\nAl Jazeera’s Tanvir Chowdhury reports from Cox’s Bazar, Bangladesh.\n\nSubscribe to our channel: http://bit.ly/AJSubscribe\nFollow us on X : https://x.com/AJEnglish\nFind us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/aljazeera\nCheck our website: http://www.aljazeera.com/\nCheck out our Instagram page: https://www.instagram.com/aljazeeraenglish/\nDownload AJE Mobile App: https://aje.news/AJEMobile\n\n#Rohingya #Myanmar #Bangladesh #CoxsBazar #ICJ",
      "chapters": []
    },
    {
      "id": "UO9YjaIceQE",
      "title": "Yemen war threatens fishing livelihoods in Aden",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-21T09:31:51Z",
      "durationSec": 99,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UO9YjaIceQE/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "The war in Yemen is threatening a fishing trade passed down through generations in the southern port city of Aden. Rising fuel prices are making trips more expensive, while a sunset-to-dawn curfew keeps fishers ashore during some of their best fishing hours. \n\nAl Jazeera’s Zein Basravi reports.\n\nSubscribe to our channel  http://bit.ly/AJSubscribe\nFollow us on X: https://x.com/AJEnglish\nFind us on Facebook https://www.facebook.com/aljazeera\nCheck our website:  http://www.aljazeera.com/\nDownload AJE Mobile App : https://aje.io/AJEMobile\n@AljazeeraEnglish\n#Aljazeeraenglish\n#News #Yemen #Aden",
      "chapters": []
    },
    {
      "id": "yOQQSvEa8b8",
      "title": "Can mediation succeed in a war-torn world? | The Art of Negotiation | EP 1",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-21T09:16:07Z",
      "durationSec": 1501,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yOQQSvEa8b8/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "As war escalates across the Middle East and Ukraine, global peace talks are under the spotlight.\n\nWe have entered a new era of hard power, with more armed conflicts across the planet than at any time since World War II.\n\nConflict negotiators who help broker peace deals say they confront an increasingly challenging landscape: tangled proxy wars, shifting power alliances and broken public trust in countries like Lebanon.\n\nAmid these growing obstacles, how can you bring bitter enemies to the negotiating table?\n\nIn this special series, Al Jazeera investigates mediation in 21st-century warzones.",
      "chapters": []
